OL,3,GNEWSASexual assault centre to stay
OL,4,Adespite cash concern
OL,5,
OL,6,FA centre for supporting victims of
OL,7,Fsexual assault will remain open despite
OL,8,Fconcerns over its funding, the
OL,9,Fgovernment has said.
OL,11,FThe Committee for Home Affairs has
OL,12,Fasked for #401,000 as part of wider
OL,13,Famendment proposals to protect
OL,14,Fvulnerable people to fund the Sexual
OL,15,FAssault Referral Centre (SARC). It was
OL,16,Fpreviously funded as a pilot scheme
OL,17,Fthrough the Government Work Plan.
OL,19,FIn 2027, the committee would support
OL,20,Fthe transition of SARC from its pilot
OL,21,Fstatus to a permanent service,
OL,22,Fofficials said.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
